{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {Notes}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {Ophelia is the daughter of Polonius, sister to Laertes, and the woman that Hamlet is in love with. She's a sweet girl but who depends on the men around her to tell her what to do, and ultimately, it leads to her untimely death. She eventually goes mad and dies by falling in a river.}\par}
